 "_why": [
  "THE portal rule (MS19, migration 590; two-sided since migration 597), one table read by both",
  "languages. A property matches portal set P when any of its ads is on P (all_sources), active",
  "or not; the status switch is judged on those ads: active = an active ad on P (active_sources),",
  "inactive = ads on P and none of them active; several portals = any of them; no portal = the",
  "property's own is_active. AND it has no ad on any EXCLUDED portal: any ad, live or ended",
  "(all_sources), or only live ones when excluded_active_only (active_sources); independent of",
  "the status switch and of a broker. tests/test_portal_rule.py runs `cases` through",
  "public.portal_status_matches, both aggregate RPCs and, for the `any` rows, the Watchdog's",
  "compiled clauses; queries.test.ts runs them through applyPortalRule. `broker_cases` are the",
  "include side over ONE broker's ads only (portal and broker together = one ad): the DB lane",
  "seeds the ads and calls the broker lookup, the SPA aggregates the broker's ads and runs the",
  "same rendering. An exclusion stays on the property under a broker, so it has no broker case."
 ],
